Triangular Faulhaber anchor expansion
HYP-2457 / T801 / OPEN-Q-079 candidate

[1] Odd Faulhaber moment identity
    Symbolic identity checks p=1..10: [(1, True), (2, True), (3, True), (4, True), (5, True), (6, True), (7, True), (8, True), (9, True), (10, True)]
    Exact formula:
      D_p(c,n)=c^p - 2*sum_{r odd} binom(p,r)c^(p-r)S_r(n)
      S_r(n)=sum_{i=1..n} i^r
    Sample integer checks:
      p=3, n=4, c=60: direct=-200, odd_moment=-200
      p=4, n=5, c=121: direct=1553761, odd_moment=1553761
      p=7, n=6, c=300: direct=4123906879466478, odd_moment=4123906879466478

[2] Anchor expansion in u=n(n+1)
    c=a+n, u=n(n+1), c_p(n)=p*u + alpha_p + beta_p/u + gamma_p/u^2 + ...
    a_p(n)=c_p(n)-n.
    alpha_p = (p - 2)*(p - 1)/(12*p)
    beta_p  = -(p - 2)*(p - 1)*(2*p**2 - 4*p - 1)/(180*p**3)
    gamma_p = (p - 2)*(p - 1)*(p + 2)*(40*p**3 - 128*p**2 + 53*p + 11)/(30240*p**5)
    Reduced series coefficients q^0..q^3 vanish for p=1..12: True
    First coefficients by p:
      p=1: alpha=0, beta=0, gamma=0
      p=2: alpha=0, beta=0, gamma=0
      p=3: alpha=1/18, beta=-1/486, gamma=7/52488
      p=4: alpha=1/8, beta=-1/128, gamma=7/8192
      p=5: alpha=1/5, beta=-29/1875, gamma=173/93750
      p=6: alpha=5/18, beta=-47/1944, gamma=623/209952
      p=7: alpha=5/14, beta=-23/686, gamma=3915/941192
      p=8: alpha=7/16, beta=-133/3072, gamma=4241/786432

    Exact p=1 and p=2 anchors recovered:
      n=1: p=1 a=c-n=1=n^2; p=2 a=c-n=3=2n^2+n
      n=2: p=1 a=c-n=4=n^2; p=2 a=c-n=10=2n^2+n
      n=3: p=1 a=c-n=9=n^2; p=2 a=c-n=21=2n^2+n
      n=4: p=1 a=c-n=16=n^2; p=2 a=c-n=36=2n^2+n
      n=5: p=1 a=c-n=25=n^2; p=2 a=c-n=55=2n^2+n
      n=6: p=1 a=c-n=36=n^2; p=2 a=c-n=78=2n^2+n

