[4] Square-pyramidal cuboid carrier
    P2(n)=1^2+...+n^2=n(n+1)(2n+1)/6.
    Six square pyramids tile the cuboid n*(n+1)*(2n+1).
    HYP-2454's first tower common sum is S1=3*P2, so the cuboid is 2*S1.
      n=1: P2=1, 6P2=6, cuboid=6, S1=3, 2S1=6
      n=2: P2=5, 6P2=30, cuboid=30, S1=15, 2S1=30
      n=3: P2=14, 6P2=84, cuboid=84, S1=42, 2S1=84
      n=4: P2=30, 6P2=180, cuboid=180, S1=90, 2S1=180
      n=5: P2=55, 6P2=330, cuboid=330, S1=165, 2S1=330
      n=6: P2=91, 6P2=546, cuboid=546, S1=273, 2S1=546
      n=7: P2=140, 6P2=840, cuboid=840, S1=420, 2S1=840

    Packing reading:
      p=1 is the square-shell carrier; p=2 is the square-pyramidal cuboid carrier.
      Higher p keeps the same u=n(n+1) carrier, but Bernoulli denominators
      move the real anchor off the integer tower by alpha_p, beta_p/u, ...

